explanation:
Since E=hf,


frac{E_{rm UV}}{E_{rm visible}}
=frac{f_{rm UV}}{f_{rm visible}}
=frac{1.2×10^{15}}{6×10^{14}}
=2.


The UV photon has twice the energy of the visible photon. The ratio is not squared because photon energy is directly proportional to frequency.

Because E=hf, the ratio of photon energies equals the ratio of frequencies:


(E_γ / E_{rm radio)}
=frac{3×10^{19}}{3×10^6}
=10^{13}.


A gamma-ray photon has 10^{13} times the energy of the specified radio-wave photon. This compares individual photons, not the total energy emitted by either source.

The frequency remains unchanged at refraction:


f=(c / lambda_{rm air)}
=(3×10^8 / 600×10^{-9)}
=5.0×10^{14} Hz.


The wavelength in glass is


lambda_g=frac{lambda_{rm air}}{n}
=(600 / 1.5)=400 nm.


